`neutron dev` runs `cargo watch -x run` when cargo-watch is installed,
otherwise `cargo run`.

The SDK (`{{.SDK.Name}}` crate) comes from the Neutron repository
(`{{.SDK.Source}}`); cargo finds the crate by name inside it and pins the
commit in `Cargo.lock`. It is not on crates.io, where `neutron` is an
unrelated crate. `cargo update -p {{.SDK.Name}}` moves to the latest commit.

## Endpoints

- `GET /api/hello` — sample route in `src/main.rs`
- `GET /health` — the SDK's contract handler: `{"status", "nucleus", "version"}`

## Configuration

Read from the environment by `Config::from_env()` (`.env` lists them; nothing
loads it automatically):

| Variable | Default |
|---|---|
| `NEUTRON_HOST` | `0.0.0.0` |
| `NEUTRON_PORT` | `8080` |
| `NEUTRON_DATABASE_URL` | unset — `/health` reports `"nucleus": "unconfigured"` |
| `NEUTRON_LOG_LEVEL` | `info` |
